# v2.4.1:
- Add cmm_set_list_button_open_tab to make a settings list button open one of your tabs
- Add cmf_log_at_location to log a location alongside an action, with no value
- Fix a settings list button field rendering as plain text you could not click
- Fix the action bar's Visible Buttons toggles not showing or hiding buttons
- Fix is_host reading false in multiplayer until the mod menu was opened
- Fix a settings list greying out when a different setting's condition changed
- The framework now does less background work, especially in multiplayer

# v2.4.0:
- The mod menu now opens with no country selected, on the country selection lobby and in observer mode, showing your last country's values. Settings can't be changed until you have a country
- Enable Debug Mode and the Mod Action Log stay usable without a country
- Add cmm_register_subtab to nest a tab under another tab, drawing a second tab row beneath the main one
- You can now click a settings group's header to collapse it, or right-click to collapse every group in the tab
- Group headers now show how many of their settings are visible
- Add cmm_register_list_button_field for a button column in a settings list
- Add cmm_register_list_text_field and cmm_set_list_text_value for a display-only text column in a settings list
- Add cmm_move_list_item to move a settings list item to a display position
- Add cmf_log_value and cmf_log_decimal_value to log a number alongside an action
- Add cmf_log_with_location, cmf_log_with_location_values, and cmf_log_with_building_location to log a location or a building with labelled values
- The action bar now stays on top of other windows
- The action bar moves above the news panel while it's expanded, and hides under a fullscreen view
- Extend cmf_suppress to cover variable maps
- Fix empty groups not hiding after switching countries
- Custom alerts now stay when left-clicked by default, with a new cmf_set_alert_remove_on_click for changing it
- Add cmf_set_alert_open_view and cmf_set_alert_open_group to open a view on alert left-click
- Add optional <root_key>_left_click localization key for the alert left-click button text
- Right-click now hides a custom alert and shift+right-click mutes it, like vanilla alerts
- Hidden and muted custom alerts can be restored from the vanilla alerts menu
- Add cmf_is_alert_hidden and cmf_is_alert_muted triggers
- Add cmf_set_alert_open_window to open your own window on alert left-click
- Clear custom alerts left behind by a mod that's no longer active
- CMM Visual Editor updated to 1.3.1

# v2.3.3:
- The mod menu now opens on a default tab the first time it's opened
- Right-click a settings list column header to apply its value to all rows
- Mod banner icons no longer show up as empty entries in the Europedia
- Fix script error spam from is_host and cmf_can_use_unrestricted_tools
- Fix settings list order not updating when changed in an existing save
- Clear stale action bar buttons when loading a save (left by a mod that's no longer active)
- Overwrite fewer vanilla keybinds when adding the mod menu keybind
- Add cmf_was_mod_active_at_game_start trigger to check whether a mod was active when the game was started
- Extend cmf_suppress to cover global variables and variable lists
- Add bom to some loc files missing it
- Update for v1.3.10

# v2.3.2:
- Empty groups, tabs, and mods now hide automatically
- Settings can now be greyed out based on a condition with a Scripted GUI is_valid block (partially implemented before, but now extended to every setting)

# v2.3.1:
- Improve mod menu performance
- Fix lobby banners becoming stale on old save games
- Update for v1.3.6

# v2.3.0:
- [b]Mod Banners:[/b] Mods can appear as banners on the pre-game lobby screen, with an icon, name, and description using cmf_register_lobby_banner.
- [b]Reset Mod to Defaults:[/b] New button to reset just the selected mod's settings. The existing button is now Reset All to Defaults.
- [b]CMM Visual Editor:[/b] Updated to support all new features including mod banners.
- [b]Visual Improvements:[/b] Updated the look of the mod menu's sliders, the mod list, and list settings.
- [b]Per-Item Field Defaults:[/b] Set a default value for an individual list item's field with cmm_set_list_field_default_for_item.
- [b]Bug Fixes:[/b] New settings list items added by a mod now appear in existing save games. A mod's settings and Reset to Defaults now apply correctly regardless of registration and configuration order.
- [b]Deprecated cmf_change_variable_map:[/b] No longer needed now that add_to_variable_map overwrites existing keys.

[b]Additionally these are the features that were snuck into the 2.2.x patches while WIP that have now been finalized:[/b]
- [b]Multi-Selector Setting:[/b] New side-by-side selector setting type.
- [b]Runtime List Field Localization:[/b] Change a list field's header, description, prefix, and postfix localization keys while the menu is open with cmm_set_list_field_localization.
- [b]Mod Detection:[/b] New cmf_is_mod_active trigger to check whether another mod is active.

# v2.2.13:
- Add cmm_set_list_field_localization which allows you to change the localization key of the header, description, prefix, and postfix with the menu open
- Refresh settings list display caches after dropdown changes so runtime localization and formatting changes show immediately
- Fix being unable to change mod playsets

# v2.2.12:
- Fix mod menu close button (broken by patch 1.3.2)

# v2.2.11:
- Update for beta v1.3.2

# v2.2.10:
- Add cmf_is_mod_active trigger to check if another mod is active

# v2.2.9:
- Fix escape to close mod menu
- Temporarily fix the vanilla mod menu's broken checkboxes

# v2.2.8:
- Fix for vanilla bug that broke the checkbox used for the mod menu

# v2.2.7:
- Update for EU5 v1.3 Pavia beta

# v2.2.6:
- Remove log viewer button from action bar
- Change mod menu action bar button text
- Add more room for slider text

# v2.2.5:
- Add new way of setting the CMF GUI marker for improved compatibility

# v2.2.4:
- Move action bar settings to mod menu
- Add mod menu toggle to the action bar
- Add multi-selector (side-by-side) setting type

# v2.2.3:
- Update for v1.2
- Add keybind for the mod menu (default 'm', can be rebinded).

# v2.2.2:
- Fix clicks on settings list items above 20
- Fix self referential dependency in metadata

# v2.2.1:
- Minor localization corrections
- Make mod menu settings open by default when no other mod has been selected.

# v2.2.0:
- [b]Mod Action Log:[/b] Shared in-game log for mod actions.
- [b]Country Transfer:[/b] CMM settings follow the player when they switch countries. cmf_on_country_transfer on_action for custom transfer logic.
- [b]Unrestricted Tools:[/b] New "Enable Unrestricted Tools" setting. Where you can use cmf_can_use_unrestricted_tools trigger to gate features behind it, and cmm_set_requires_unrestricted_tools_enabled to lock individual settings. Can be used for balance breaking changes, host tools, etc.
- [b]Settings Lists:[/b] New read-only data field type. New Prefix/postfix value formatting with sign-conditional variants. Per-item row hiding.
- [b]Mod Removal:[/b] When a mod is disabled, its settings disappear from existing save games.
- [b]GUI Macros:[/b] New Nand, Nor, and Xor logical operator macros.
- [b]Performance:[/b] CMM performance improved by ~3x.
- [b]Bug Fixes:[/b] on_game_start_after_lobby no longer fires on loads where CMF is inactive.
- [b]Improved Vanilla Top-Level Widget Overrides:[/b] Top-level vanilla widgets like lateralviews can only be overridden by replacing the whole file they're defined in, which normally forces you to copy every type and template in that file too. CMF now includes extracted copies of those definitions so your override only needs the top-level widget itself.

# v2.1.2:
- Fix GlorpUI compatability on existing save games

# v2.1.1:
- Correct _player_country to _human_country on some on_action hooks

# v2.1.0:
- [b]Post-Lobby On-Action Hooks:[/b] New lifecycle hooks (on_game_start_after_lobby, on_game_load, on_game_load_after_lobby) that fire after country selection, with human country variants. Solves the vanilla limitation where on_game_start fires before the lobby.
- [b]Mod Auto-Enabler:[/b] Dependency check popup on the main menu that automatically enables CMF or opens the Workshop when missing.
- [b]Per-Item List Field Disabling:[/b] Hide specific field columns for specific items in list settings (cmm_disable_list_field_for_item / cmm_enable_list_field_for_item).
- [b]Variable Map Utilities:[/b] New cmf_change_variable_map, cmf_change_local_variable_map, and cmf_change_global_variable_map effects for safe variable map mutation.
- [b]Bug Fixes:[/b] Fixed monthly/yearly hook scoping and unset scope errors.
- [b]CMM Visual Editor (v1.1.0):[/b] Added support for per-item field disabling and fixed list iteration boilerplate naming.

# v2.0.0:
- [b]Community Mod Menu (CMM):[/b] A shared in-game mod settings window with toggle, button, numeric, slider (double click to drag), dropdown, text (singleplayer-only), and list settings. Includes per-mod tabs, groups, search, global settings with host-only multiplayer editing, and Reset to Defaults.
- [b]CMM Visual Editor:[/b] Browser-based tool for creating CMM settings without manual coding. Includes live preview and drag-and-drop ordering.
- [b]is_host Trigger:[/b] Check if the current country is controlled by the host player.
- [b]cmf_suppress Effect:[/b] Suppress "used but never set" and "set but never used" engine warnings with a single effect call.
- [b]Player Country Hooks:[/b] Shared on_actions (cmf_yearly_human_country_pulse, cmf_monthly_human_country_pulse) that fire for each human player's country on yearly and monthly pulses.
- [b]Community Mod Toolkit (CMT):[/b] Companion development tools: mod template, workshop uploader, and automated translation.
- [b]Unified Callback System:[/b] Custom Alerts and Action Bar now use a single cmf_on_callback on_action.
- [b]Scripted GUIs are no longer required:[/b] Alerts and action bar elements only need a Scripted GUI for conditional visibility or enabled state.
- [b]Documentation:[/b] Full documentation on the [url=https://github.com/Europa-Universalis-5-Modding-Co-op/community-mod-framework/wiki]GitHub Wiki[/url] and quick reference on the [url=https://eu5.paradoxwikis.com/Community_Mod_Framework]Paradox Wiki[/url].
